<div class="wp-block-group tt-wrap"><!-- wp:paragraph {"className":"tt-ilede"} -->
<p class="tt-ilede">Entrusting your child to an off-site school journey requires clarity, open communication, and predictable arrangements. We provide detailed information from the first briefing evening until the coach pulls back up to the school gates.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>
<!-- /wp:group --></div>
<!-- /wp:group -->

<!-- wp:group {"className":"tt-sec tt-isec","layout":{"type":"default"},"align":"full"} -->
<div class="wp-block-group alignfull tt-sec tt-isec"><!-- wp:group {"className":"tt-wrap","layout":{"type":"default"}} -->
<div class="wp-block-group tt-wrap"><!-- wp:heading {"level":2,"className":"tt-h2 tt-isec__h"} -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading tt-h2 tt-isec__h">Questions parents ask</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:group {"className":"tt-qas","layout":{"type":"default"}} -->
<div class="wp-block-group tt-qas"><!-- wp:details {"className":"tt-qa"} -->
<details class="wp-block-details tt-qa"><summary>When do we receive updates during the trip?</summary><!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Communication begins six weeks before departure at the school parents evening, where itineraries and safety guidelines are shared. Two weeks prior, you receive the definitive packing list. On day one at eight fifteen, we confirm that all students are safely aboard the coach. Every evening at twenty-one hundred hours, we send a direct message detailing the day activities, arrival at accommodation, and next-day plans, culminating in arrival updates when returning to the school gate.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>
<!-- /wp:details --><!-- wp:details {"className":"tt-qa"} -->
<details class="wp-block-details tt-qa"><summary>How does the three-part payment schedule work?</summary><!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>To help families plan household budgets comfortably, trip costs are divided into three distinct instalments over the academic year. An initial deposit of twenty percent is due upon booking to secure transport and accommodation reservations. A second payment of forty percent is payable by the conclusion of the spring term. The remaining balance of forty percent is due six weeks prior to departure, ensuring all accounts are settled without last-minute stress.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>
<!-- /wp:details --><!-- wp:details {"className":"tt-qa"} -->
<details class="wp-block-details tt-qa"><summary>How are medical and dietary needs managed?</summary><!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Every student medical requirement, allergy, and dietary accommodation is logged during the initial registration process in spring. Tour leaders cross-reference this medical sheet against accommodation meal plans and pre-booked restaurant arrangements weeks in advance. During the tour, leaders carry individual medical overview summaries at all times. Any prescribed medications are managed according to the school protocols agreed during your initial parent consent submissions, ensuring student wellbeing remains continuous.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>
<!-- /wp:details --><!-- wp:details {"className":"tt-qa"} -->
<details class="wp-block-details tt-qa"><summary>Who is looking after the students on the trip?</summary><!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Students are supervised by their school teachers alongside professional tour leaders from our Ashby Vale team. We operate on a strict staffing ratio of one leader for every ten students, ensuring consistent oversight during travel, site visits, and mealtimes. Every leader is briefed on emergency protocols and group logistics, and all staff have direct, uninterrupted access to our twenty-four-hour operational duty line throughout the entire journey.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>
<!-- /wp:details --><!-- wp:details {"className":"tt-qa"} -->
<details class="wp-block-details tt-qa"><summary>What happens if a student is unwell or needs assistance?</summary><!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If a pupil requires medical attention or becomes unwell, our tour leaders and school staff follow an established response protocol. Minor issues are managed immediately using our emergency contact logs and school-approved medical files. For anything requiring clinical assessment, leaders contact local healthcare services and notify parents within one hour through the school lead teacher, while our twenty-four-hour Ashby Vale duty line coordinates logistical support.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>
<!-- /wp:details --><!-- wp:details {"className":"tt-qa"} -->
<details class="wp-block-details tt-qa"><summary>What luggage and clothing should students pack?</summary><!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Two weeks before departure, families receive a specific packing list tailored to the destination, climate, and planned itinerary. We advise one compact suitcase or duffel bag and a sturdy day backpack for daily excursions, water bottles, and notebooks. Pupils require practical, weather-appropriate clothing without designer logos, comfortable walking shoes broken in before departure, and a light waterproof jacket. Passports and national identification documents are collected and checked prior to departure.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>
<!-- /wp:details --></div>
<!-- /wp:group --></div>
<!-- /wp:group --></div>
<!-- /wp:group -->

